Driven by the principles of chemical reactivity and equilibrium, the industrial gases industry provides essential supplies like nitrogen, oxygen, and hydrogen to manufacturers. These gases serve as foundational raw materials or reagents across the chemical manufacturing industry. This section addresses chemical equilibrium principles and calculations applied to gas-phase reactions. In particular, it addresses the idea of percent dissociation as another way to quantify the extent of a reaction. Percent dissociation measures the proportion of an original reagent that decomposes to form products

